WEBVTT

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.510
<i>That day,</i>

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:12.930
<i>that time...</i>

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.760
<i>That was a precious moment for me.</i>

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.810
<i>My close, dear friends risked their lives</i>

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.020
<i>in order to save mine.</i>

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:30.440
<i>Also, there was a woman</i>
<i>who assisted us helpless children.</i>

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.280
<i>She called herself Milo.</i>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.530
<i>I never saw her again after that.</i>

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.790
<i>But what happened that day</i>
<i>is seared into my memory.</i>

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.880
Same dream again.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.340
Let's get started.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.390
<i>I was pathetic back then.</i>

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.350
<i>All I did was cry</i>
<i>and rely on everyone else.</i>

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.810
<i>I need to be stronger next time.</i>

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:06.900
<i>Milo told us then that one day,</i>
<i>a terrible danger would befall us.</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:07.980
I'm off, Mikio.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.270
-Take care.
-<i>If so...</i>

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:13.860
Morning, Lu!

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.290
Don't ride so fast on this road!

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.040
Hey, come back here!

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.300
Daisuke, not again!

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.460
Don't act like you didn't hit her!

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.340
Bastard!

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:39.180
-How dare you hurt Lu in front--
-What are you doing, Daisuke?

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.180
I'm so sorry. Are you all right?

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.020
What are you apologizing for?

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.890
-You went too far!
-I just...

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.400
That bastard!

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:54.690
Don't you dare pass through here again!
Next time I see you, I'll--

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.110
Take a hint!
Your heroic antics are annoying!

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.700
<i>But, back then,</i>

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.330
<i>Milo told me...</i>

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.370
<i>I was the only one capable</i>
<i>of protecting everyone.</i>

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:12.500
<i>Yes, this is my calling.</i>

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:13.920
<i>It's my destiny.</i>

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.310
<i>Why are you here, Ms. Yumiko?</i>

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:57.440
Neither of us have a choice.
Mr. Sato is not around today.

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.690
I'm a certified school counselor too,
you know.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:05.990
Besides, it should be "Ms. Yazawa."
Don't call me by my first name.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:08.950
But nobody here calls you that.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:12.660
Anyway, Dojima,
I heard you got into trouble again.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.000
I did not!<i></i>Lu was in trouble,
so I had to protect her.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.840
Oh, I get it.
It's the same thing as always.

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:20.840
Don't mock me!

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.840
Sorry. I didn't mean it that way.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:28.560
I also heard you turned in
your career planning sheet blank.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:29.560
Yes.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.600
Mr. Ito was worried about you.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.480
You have good grades,
so he doesn't understand why.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:39.440
I just can't think about the future.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.900
I'm serious.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.950
You can't even decide
whether you want to go to college or work?

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.660
<i>I know you can get into university</i>
<i>without taking a test here.</i>

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:52.120
<i>Well, you see, I'm planning on</i>
<i>protecting everyone if something happens.</i>

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:55.460
That's my duty and destiny.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.790
I see.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.760
You were friends with Asano
and the others in the past, right?

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:06.010
That was back when I was
in elementary school.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:09.810
Well, I suppose we still spend
a lot of time together.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:18.560
<i>Hey, everyone!</i>

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.480
<i>-How is it going?</i>
-I'm serious.

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:23.440
<i>-It's now time for the lunch broadcast.</i>
-What's wrong, Marimari?

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:27.570
-You were staring into space.
<i>-</i>Do you want to go to the cafeteria today?

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.820
Oh, no.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:31.120
Or is it about Dojima?

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:35.290
He's a real creep, isn't he?

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:36.870
Only last week,

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.330
a man was asking Marimari
for directions

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.710
<i>and he suddenly knocked him down, right?</i>
<i>The guy ended up with fractured ribs.</i>

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:47.680
<i>Luckily, he was a reasonable guy</i>
<i>and didn't press charges.</i>

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.930
<i>Yes, but I got really mad at Daisuke.</i>

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:53.520
<i>Of course! Does that bother you?</i>

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:57.480
I suppose you guys have been friends
since elementary school.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.690
-Oh, really?
-Oh, right, Riko,

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:01.860
you came here in middle school,
so you wouldn't know.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:05.280
Marimari, Dojima, Keisaku,
and the Steiner twins...

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:07.860
-2You mean Gai and Lu?
-Right.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:12.410
The five of them always hung out together.
They were a close-knit group.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:37.600
Yes!

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.600
-All right, that's it for the first half!
-That was great!

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:42.190
Why don't you try to become a pro too?

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.270
I'm not like my older brother.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.610
What's wrong?

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:49.280
I figured you would run in
from your position.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:55.040
-Gai!
-Daisuke!

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.950
I heard you caused trouble
for my little sister again.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:01.290
Trouble?
No, I was just trying to protect Lu.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:02.500
That again?

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:05.800
Listen, something bad is definitely
going to happen!

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.710
You should know that too, Gai.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.760
You know what?
You need to stop it with your delusions.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:13.970
-But Milo said--
-We could have heard it wrong!

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.180
We were in elementary school.

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:19.480
Besides, we don't even know
if Milo was real.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:21.730
Milo is real.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:24.650
Something bad will happen!

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:26.320
How long are you going to keep--

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.450
Enough of that!

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:35.950
Hey.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.790
Did you get into a fight with Gai?

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.330
He doesn't get it.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.500
Whatever. I'm the one
who will protect everyone anyway.

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:51.630
What does Marimari say
about Lu, the danger, and other stuff?

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.550
Who knows? She hangs out more
with her female friends lately--

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:57.470
Hey, what are you doing?

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.310
You're carrying stuff like this
around again?

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.390
It's called a butterfly knife, right?

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:03.730
You're totally off.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.900
It's a carbon steel folding knife.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.110
You also use that pen that turns
into a weird weapon, right?

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.320
A tactical pen.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:15.320
And you've got emergency provisions
at home. What's with you, man?

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:17.580
Are you part of special ops?
Or a commando?

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.660
Or are you the weapons dealer
next to the dungeon?

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:24.830
Hey, why don't you stop
doing those things?

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:29.670
If you spend every minute of the day
on edge worrying about some crisis,

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:31.760
you'll go crazy, you'll be a nutcase!

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:33.090
Quit lecturing me.

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:35.590
It's just a friendly advice, Daisuke.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.100
Everyone is worried.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.930
We're second-year high school students.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.100
You can't pass it off anymore
as teenage angst.

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:42.140
I'm just...

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:47.480
I'm an unlucky guy, but you're not.
Quit trying so hard to heal those wounds.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.820
Don't push yourself so hard.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.320
None of us are kids
like we were back then.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:56.870
<i>Yes, it seems the children were a group</i>
<i>of friends in elementary school.</i>

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:57.990
7 YEARS AGO
YEAR 2010

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.990
<i>Right. From a private school in Tokyo.</i>

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.910
<i>I'm at the house</i>
<i>of the missing child, Daisuke.</i>

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.210
<i>It seems he got lost</i>
<i>at the summer festival.</i>

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:09.380
-Why did Daisuke...
-Don't worry, Marin.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.210
I'm sure they will find him.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:19.300
Hello? Who is this?

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.260
It's me. Daisuke.

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:22.970
<i>Daisuke!</i>

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:25.140
Hey, Daisuke, where are you?

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:29.860
He wants everyone to come.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:34.440
Marimari, Keisaku, Gai, and Lu.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:39.570
If you don't all come,
he says he'll kill me!

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:43.830
<i>They'll kill me if you tell the cops</i>
<i>about this phone call!</i>

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:46.410
Hello?

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.000
What should we do?

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.380
Maybe we should tell the cops.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:51.460
We can't.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:53.710
Yes, it will put Daisuke in danger.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:57.470
Then, how about
we tell Daisuke's grandparents?

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.740
-Help!
-Keep quiet.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.450
Who are you?

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.080
Are you Gai and Keisaku?

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.540
Don't be scared. My name is Milo.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:30.960
I'm here to help Daisuke.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:34.130
Wait. How did you know us?

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:45.640
I'll take care of this corpse,
so don't worry.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:50.150
You just have to tell the police
what I told you to say earlier.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:54.070
You went searching for Daisuke
on your own.

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:58.780
Dai had been kidnapped,
but we found him in the woods nearby.

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:01.990
But we don't know
where the kidnapper went.

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.870
That's right. I know you can do it.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:07.290
You can't tell anyone about me.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.210
Do you understand?

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:11.540
No one will believe you anyway.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:12.920
Thank you!

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:14.710
Thank you, miss.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.380
Listen to me, Daisuke.
This is a prophecy.

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:24.010
The five of you will someday
find yourselves in terrible danger.

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:27.060
Only you will be able to protect them.

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:31.230
No matter what happens, don't forget that.
You are going to protect everyone.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:35.730
<i>That was a precious time for me.</i>

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:38.650
<i>It was only an instant,</i>

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:40.490
<i>but because of that,</i>

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:43.070
<i>it felt like an eternity to me.</i>

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.040
Who's calling me this late?

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:50.910
"The end and the beginning"?

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.500
BEING IN SHIBUYA

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:55.710
IS DANGEROUS

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.340
BEING IN SHIBUYA TOMORROW IS DANGEROUS.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:00.260
BUT THE SIX OF US NEED TO BE THERE
EVEN IF A DREADFUL BATTLE BEGINS.

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:01.970
The time has finally come.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.060
Get away from Shibuya?

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:16.110
Well, there were these rumors online

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:19.440
about some accident or crime
happening in Shibuya today.

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:22.400
I figured you should be careful
just in case, Mikio.

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:23.700
Yes, but...

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:27.740
I just got off night duty,
so I was going to stay at home.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:32.120
-Don't you have errands elsewhere?
-What? You don't want me at home?

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:36.170
Oh, I get it.
You want to bring a girl over.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:38.290
An opportunity has finally
come knocking on--

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:39.960
No, that's not it. I'm serious.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.420
Say Daisuke,

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:45.680
are you sure you wouldn't rather
live with your mom and dad?

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:49.390
Like I told you before,
I don't want to leave my friends.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:52.230
This place is closer to school too.
So, if it's okay with you--

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:54.270
I'm fine with it if you are.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:57.110
Thank you! I'm off then!

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:03.240
He seems overly excited today.

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.740
<i>That was the song requested by Saito,</i>

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:07.990
Wheat Field for the Old Queen.

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:10.370
<i>-That's a great song.</i>
-I knew it.

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:12.370
I knew I could count on you
in a critical time.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:14.790
"Critical time"? So it was you?

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.790
-You're going too far.
-What?

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:18.670
BEING IN SHIBUYA IS DANGEROUS TOMORROW.

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:20.250
Explain, Daisuke.

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:23.670
What is there to explain?
Something is about to happen--

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:26.880
Don't be ridiculous!

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:31.060
-You--
-Wait!

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:33.270
I know you don't like confrontation,

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:35.270
but he went too far this time.

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:39.900
No, I agree that sending a weird message
in the middle of the night is troublesome.

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:42.150
-But still--
-Sending a message? Me?

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:43.230
Damn it!

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.650
Daisuke's been acting strange
ever since that time!

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:48.820
Talking about protecting everyone
and "destiny" stuff!

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:50.950
Because that's what Milo told us!

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.830
We promised we would forget
everything that happened!

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.410
When are you going to let it go?

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.460
You're always worried
something will happen,

00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:00.750
but if you watch the news,
stuff happens somewhere every day.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.090
You're being a pain, Daisuke!

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:04.590
But I'm not the one who sent the message!

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:06.420
I believe what Milo said.

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:09.050
Someday, something will happen.
And today--

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:27.990
<i>We are experiencing a power outage</i>
<i>due to an earthquake.</i>

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:30.370
<i>We are currently working to--</i>

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:33.410
-What was that? An earthquake?
-It was weird though.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:35.660
-Daisuke!
-This guy!

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:46.710
What happened to the building?

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:48.720
Why is that part gone?

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:50.840
This is it.

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:55.060
-You mean the thing Milo told us?
-Yes. This is it, Gai!

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:57.560
This is it! This is what she meant!

00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:58.980
This?

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:00.730
What exactly happened?

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:03.150
Don't ask me.

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:05.150
So, what should we do next?

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:06.820
"What should we do next"?

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:11.320
What is this?
Where's the rest of the building?

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.160
-Terrorism?
-My phone is not working.

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:14.950
Someone, get the teacher.

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:17.200
-Should we try the emergency call service?
-Yes.

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:20.120
-Where are you going?
-Why does it matter?

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:24.040
I'm going to go home to check on my mom.
Marimari, I'll be back soon.

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:25.000
Okay.

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:28.710
-Where are we going?
-The store.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:31.340
Our school should have
emergency provisions.

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:32.680
It won't be enough.

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:48.110
<i>I thought I had prepared myself</i>
<i>for something like this.</i>

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:49.820
There's no reception here either!

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:50.820
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:53.870
<i>Now it's happening,</i>
<i>it's like my brain stopped working!</i>

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.200
What's that?

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:58.740
Is it an alarm?

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:00.910
What's that?

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:01.830
Where?

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:02.960
Over there. See?

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:06.500
There's something.
Did it fall from the sky?

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:10.210
-It probably came up from the underground.
<i>-</i>Is it a bomb?

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:12.590
It looks like a sculpture.

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.680
Daisuke! Hey, Daisuke!

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:45.920
Let me go!

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:49.800
Help!

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:54.300
Marimari!

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:57.180
Ms. Yumiko!

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:01.680
-I'm sorry!
-Ms. Yumiko!

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:04.140
Open the door!

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:06.100
Ms. Yumiko! Open the door!

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:08.400
Ms. Yumiko! Damn it, Ms. Yumiko!

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:14.030
<i>I made a vow to protect everyone.</i>
<i>I thought it was my duty and destiny.</i>

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:17.200
<i>But this is insane!</i>

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:18.490
<i>We're going to die.</i>

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:20.950
<i>If this keeps up, we'll definitely die!</i>

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:22.120
<i>You bastard!</i>

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:24.410
<i>No.</i>

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:26.460
<i>I don't want to die!</i>

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:28.830
Let's jump too!

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.550
If we land on our feet at this height,
we should be...

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:42.180
Stay away!

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:43.140
Hey!

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.060
Hey, over here!

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:52.230
<i>Crap! Marimari is...</i>

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:54.490
<i>But my legs...</i>

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:55.950
<i>They won't move.</i>

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:03.490
<i>I thought I could handle this.</i>

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:06.120
<i>I'm so helpless.</i>

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:17.050
I'm Milo,
a Balancer for District Four AHRV HQ.

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:18.630
How many survivors?

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:22.350
Milo? Did you say "Milo"?
You look the same as before!

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:23.970
You knew me?

00:18:24.430 --> 00:18:26.430
I see. So, it's just as predicted.

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:28.600
"Predicted"?

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:40.530
She knocked it out?

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:46.910
-Did you defeat it?
<i>-</i>No, not with this level of attack.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.330
Then I'll finish it. Let me use that!

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:51.080
-Who are you?
-It's Daisuke!

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:52.750
Daisuke Dojima--

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:54.210
Dojima?

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:58.840
I'll protect everyone, as you said!
I promise I will do it this time!

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:04.890
In that case,
I have a weapon especially for you.

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.270
You can use that.

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:07.560
My own weapon?

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:11.690
What's happening, Milo?
Why did you suddenly show up?

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:13.440
You are Marin Temari, right?

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:16.320
I will explain later.

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:21.450
Take the rest of the survivors
and evacuate.

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:24.370
Hide in a sturdy building,
where a thing that size won't fit.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:26.740
If you hide, it won't find you
for a while.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:28.040
How long is "a while"?

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:29.620
Daisuke, you said?

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:32.880
-Come.
-Wait...

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:38.210
Hurry!

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:44.720
What's that?

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:46.680
A String Puppet.

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:49.310
Our secret weapon.

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:53.230
-We can battle Revisions with this.
-What?

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.940
Revisions.
That's what the enemy is called.

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:57.150
The enemy?

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:00.780
Shouldn't the police or army
do something about that?

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:04.120
<i>Was your house okay?</i>

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:05.070
Yes.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:09.160
Is it true that Milo suddenly showed up
and took Daisuke with him?

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:13.620
-Yes. But Milo didn't seem to know us.
-She didn't know us?

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:17.380
Yes. The way she talked
seemed different too.

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:22.720
You want me to get in this thing?

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.890
You're not wearing a suit,
but don't worry.

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:27.680
It should be perfectly tuned
to your cerebral nerves.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.520
The Man-Machine Interface will
take care of the rest and help you pilot.

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:31.640
Hurry!

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:33.600
The Civilian is about to wake up.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:39.360
<i>Anti-Revisions</i><i>Wearable Combat System,</i>
<i>String Puppet.</i>

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:42.450
<i>Cerebral nerve mapping</i>
<i>compatible with the pilot.</i>

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:44.610
<i>Daisuke Dojima confirmed.</i>

00:22:21.750 --> 00:22:24.630
<i>We didn't understand anything</i>
<i>that was happening.</i>

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:26.260
<i>But one thing</i>

00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:27.720
<i>is clear.</i>

00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:33.560
<i>I've been living my life since that day</i>
<i>preparing for this moment!</i>

00:22:34.930 --> 00:22:39.310
<i>Daisuke Dojima, welcome to the year 2388.</i>

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:42.150
<i>The danger you must overcome,</i>

00:22:42.480 --> 00:22:47.440
<i>the enemy you vowed to save everyone from,</i>
<i>is the future.</i>

00:22:50.070 --> 00:22:52.070
Subtitle translation by Emily Noguchi
